vo_frame_output.c: read the NV12 range from params.repr.levels.

The 0001 patch tested img->params.color.levels, but in the pinned
mpv 0.41.0 + libplacebo 7.387.0 combination pl_color_space has no
levels member — the range lives in struct pl_color_repr, which
mp_image_params carries as params.repr (video/mp_image.h).  CI round
11: "vo_frame_output.c:201:36: error: no member named 'levels' in
'struct pl_color_space'".  The file's only other member access of
this kind was checked the same way; this was the sole misuse.

diff --git a/video/out/vo_frame_output.c b/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
--- a/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
@@ -199,6 +199,6 @@
     switch (img->imgfmt) {
     case IMGFMT_NV12:
-        ostype = img->params.color.levels == PL_COLOR_LEVELS_FULL
+        ostype = img->params.repr.levels == PL_COLOR_LEVELS_FULL
             ? kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8BiPlanarFullRange
             : kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8BiPlanarVideoRange;
         break;
